CHANGE 7 — CAMERA FRAMING AND THE DOUBLE-UNIT BUG (the real cause)
  SYMPTOM: the viewer rendered a flat grey field. Pixel histogram proved it:
    76,765 of 76,800 pixels in one brightness band. Not a framing problem.
  THE GAZEBO GUI CONFIRMED IT: opening ao-sim-fabrication-gui-gz showed the
  ground grid and NOTHING else. No building geometry had ever rendered.

  ROOT CAUSE: a DOUBLE inch->metre conversion.
    The Collada exports declare   <unit meter="0.0254" name="inch"/>
    and the world ALSO applied    <scale>0.0254 0.0254 0.0254</scale>
  Gazebo honours the DAE <unit> element, so the scale was applied a second time:
  0.0254 x 0.0254 = 0.000645. The 7.87 m plant was being drawn 6.5 mm across -
  sub-pixel, therefore invisible. The collision boxes were correct the whole
  time, which is why the boned extents looked right while nothing rendered.
  FIX: <scale>1.0 1.0 1.0</scale> on all three meshes. Do NOT put the 0.0254
  back - the conversion is already in the file.

  PROOF (single-variable test, massing only, scale 1.0 vs 0.0254):
    dark pixels 35 -> 16,881 ; all three meshes -> 17,667 dark, 23% of frame.

  ALSO ADDED: explicit <material> on building_massing, conveyor_system and
  robot_arms. They had none, so they lit almost identically to the 0.7-grey
  background and were hard to read even once visible.

  CAMERA, from the boned cell-massing envelope (0,0,0)-(7.874,4.831072,2.0574):
    centre (3.937, 2.4155, 1.0287)
    h_fov 1.047 rad -> v_fov 46.8 deg at the default 4:3 aspect
    fill distance = hypot(7.874,4.831072)/2 / tan(h_fov/2) = 8.00 m
    FINAL POSE  8.837 7.316 5.030 0 0.5236 -2.3562
    (30 deg elevation, 45 deg azimuth, camera 5.03 m up vs a 2.06 m building)
  SAVED AS THE DEFAULT IN BOTH PLACES:
    GAZEBO/worlds/factory.world  - both the camera_rig sensor and the <gui>
                                   camera, kept byte-identical as the file
                                   requires
    ~/.local/share/ao-simulation/gui-home/.gz/sim/10/gui.config line 44
                                   <camera_pose>8.837 7.316 5.030 0 0.5236
                                   -2.3562</camera_pose>
    (backup of the previous gui.config: /tmp/gui.config.bak)

