  NOT DONE — BLUE DOORS. Cannot be separated reliably from this export.
  massing_fab.dae has no semantic part names (anonymous group_0..group_25), and
  running the splitter on it returns a degenerate signature - every part comes
  back as a CUBE (150x150x150, 161x161x161, 152x152x152 ...), so the AABB
  computation is not resolving real per-part geometry for that file. There is
  therefore no way to tell a door from a wall. Delivering it would mean either
  re-exporting the SketchUp model with named groups, or fixing the splitter's
  AABB handling for that file. I did not guess a colour onto the wrong
  geometry.

