  VIEWER BUGS FOUND WHILE VERIFYING (both were "the dropdown does nothing"):
  1. The change handler set the channel variable but never sent unsubscribe or
     subscribe, so the picture never moved.
  2. Even after that, stale frames kept overdrawing the canvas. A foxglove
     binary frame does not identify its channel in the payload - the
     SUBSCRIPTION ID is carried at BYTE 1 (a frame for subscription 11 starts
     1,11,0,0; confirmed by subscribing with ids 100-103 and reading the byte
     back). The viewer now filters on that byte AND takes a FRESH subscription
     id on every selection, so any in-flight frame from the previous channel
     fails the filter immediately.
  3. The dropdown listed /rosout, /parameter_events and the bridge's own
     sysinfo. Now filtered to /factory/camera/* only.

  PROOF THE FOUR ARE GENUINELY DIFFERENT (per-channel wire hashes, each
  subscribed alone with its own id):
    left  3750641230 | image 3723722013 | edge 2381276890 | above 3987311982
  Verified visually in the browser for all four.

CHANGE 6 — 2026-10-02/03: manual viewport resize + 7 cameras aimed at boned cells
OPERATOR REQUEST: make the 3D view manually resizable; review camera locations
(they were aimed at the building centre, not the arms) and add 3 elevation views.

A. MANUAL RESIZE (GAZEBO/portal/viewer/index.html)
   - #viewwrap gained CSS resize:both (drag bottom-right corner).
   - Numeric width/height inputs, clamped 240..1920 x 180..1080, plus Fit/Full.
   - Canvas backing store follows the wrapper (crisp, not stretched); image is
     scaled into it preserving aspect ratio.
   - ResizeObserver guarded against ratcheting: only a genuinely different size
     is written back, and the element's own measured width is never echoed into
     the style that produced it.

B. CAMERA RE-AIM — the real fault
   All four original views were aimed at the MASSING centre (3.937, 2.4155,
   1.0287). The robot arms are boned at cell-arms centre (6.821, 3.534, 1.151)
   (GAZEBO/sim/boning.yaml:38-39, extent 0.840 x 1.672391 x 1.238532). They are
   ~2.9 m off the building centre, so no arm view ever contained the arms.

C. 7 CAMERAS, all standoff derived from boned extents
   arms   : 1.9 m, 22 deg elevation, cell-arms centre
            ne(az45) n(az90) se(az135) + a 4th at az60/38deg
   elev   : arms 3.8 m/65deg, conveyor 3.4 m/65deg, massing 8.6 m/70deg
   Standoff formula: d = projected_half_width / tan(h_fov/2), h_fov = 1.047 rad.

D. MEASURED OCCLUSION MAP for cell-arms (boned x 6.401..7.241, y 2.698..4.370)
   CLEAR  : az 45, 60, 90, 135
   BLOCKED: az 0   (camera outside x_max 7.874 -> building's own east wall)
   BLOCKED: az 180 (camera inside a wall; flat brown fill)
   BLOCKED: az 225 (interior partition fills frame)
   BLOCKED: az 315 (conveyor fills frame)
   The cell is in the building's north-east corner, so south/west quadrants have
   no line of sight. This map is recorded in factory.world next to the camera so
   the next session does not repeat four failed placements.

E. VIEWER BUGS FOUND AND FIXED (all caught by pixel inspection, not assumption)
   1. drawImage(canvas, ...) copied the visible canvas onto ITSELF. The
      unscaled native-resolution frame survived in the top-left corner of every
      upscaled view. Fixed with an offscreen decodeCanvas + a fillRect clear.
      I introduced this bug myself and shipped it once - it rendered the canvas
      fully black because the 9-arg drawImage overload needs source w/h.
      Caught by calling render() on a live frame and reading the thrown error,
      because the per-frame catch was swallowing it.
   2. unsubscribe used `subscriptions:[...]`. The foxglove protocol uses a FLAT
      `subscriptionIds:[id]` for unsubscribe. The bridge logged
      "Invalid message ... missing field `subscriptionIds`" on every channel
      change and silently kept the old subscription, so the dropdown changed the
      label but never the picture. This is the same class of bug as the
      subscription-id-in-byte-1 filter fixed earlier.

F. VERIFICATION (live, via Playwright against 127.0.0.1:8765/viewer)
   - Server advertises 8 cameras after restart.
   - Bridge: 8 GZ->ROS bridges, 0 failures.
   - arms_ne / arms_n / arms_se / arms_e: arms (orange) clearly in frame.
   - elev_arms: whole arms cell in frame (widened from 2.9 m/70deg, which cut
     the cell off at the top edge).
   - elev_conveyor: conveyor + arms both legible.
   - elev_massing: full plan view of the building.
   - Selection changes now actually move the subscription (hz 3.5+ on switch).

