view DIRECTLY FROM THE SIDE, not at an angle.
FIX: all three recomputed with pitch EXACTLY 0.0000 -- camera level with the subject
centre, optical axis horizontal and face-on to one side of each cell. narrow
horizontal_fov 0.6 rad (was 1.047) to flatten perspective.
  camera_elev_arms      N elevation  d=2.67m  6.821  6.203 1.151  0 0.0000 -1.5708
  camera_elev_conveyor  S elevation  d=4.38m  6.073 -2.042 1.029  0 0.0000  1.5708
  camera_elev_massing   E elevation  d=7.81m 11.746  2.416 1.029  0 0.0000  3.1416
STANDBOFF: d = max((across_frame_width/2)/tan(h_fov/2), (height/2)/tan(v_fov/2)).
  CRITICAL: across-frame width is the axis PERPENDICULAR to the view direction, not
  the extent named in boning. A N/S elevation's frame width is the X extent; an E/W
  elevation's is the Y extent. First attempt used the named extent for both and put
  the east elevation 16.664m out -- it framed a distant slab in 1/3 of the frame.
VERIFIED: XML valid; 8 cameras advertised after restart; screenshot of each of the
