CHANGE 10 - elev_arms framing, from boned datum to measured as-built centroid
Issue: README work item 70 recorded that elev_arms framed the boned arms-cell
datum, which is narrower than the as-built arm cluster, so the arms sat
off-centre and the building wall intruded at frame left.

Method (no estimating from a render):
1. Extracted the true arms AABB from GAZEBO/models/factory_assets/meshes/arms.dae
   vertex positions, transformed by the visual pose in factory.world.
   Measured: min (5.9813, 1.8617, 0.5315)  max (6.8213, 3.5341, 1.1508)
2. The boned joint_origin was (6.401314, 2.697865, 1.150797) -- the as-built
   centroid. boning.yaml cell-arms origin was (6.821, 3.534, 1.151), i.e. the
   cell's far corner, NOT a centre. That is why the datum was wrong.
3. Rewrote boning.yaml cell-arms so origin is the as-built centroid, and
   recomputed every camera that aimed at it.
4. Wrote an explicit line-of-sight checker (ray vs the world collision boxes)
   and swept azimuth x distance x elevation for a vantage that (a) has clear
   LOS to the arms and (b) contains the WHOLE measured AABB inside the frame.

